  "definitions": {
    "detections": "Per sequence: results[].decision.predicted_taxon with decision.taxon_rank when the orchestrator wrote a decision, otherwise the legacy results[].predicted_taxon (rank not recorded). Sequences with contamination_flagged = true are excluded. A taxon is present in a sample when at least one remaining sequence is assigned to it. Detections are those sequences in the sample's newest analysis, counted at the sample's timestamp.",
    "interpretation": "Counts of when samples were taken and what they contained. A daily or weekly pattern here describes the sampling schedule unless sampling was evenly spread; it is not by itself evidence of an organism's activity cycle.",
    "sample": "One sample = one upload in scope (owner, upload created_at within [date_from, date_to], UTC, both days inclusive). Its contents are read from its newest stored analysis; older re-runs of the same upload are not counted. An upload with no stored analysis yet is still a sample, with no contents: rhythms places it by its timestamp with 0 detections (totals.uploads counts every sample, totals.samples_analysed those with an analysis), and co-occurrence, which can only pair taxa from analysed samples, reports uploads_in_scope for every sample and samples for the analysed ones.",
    "timestamp": "Each upload is placed by its collected_at when recorded, otherwise by its upload created_at; the two are counted separately (uploads_collected_at / uploads_upload_time).",
    "timezone": "Hours and weekdays are in UTC, not local or solar time at the sampling site. A collection date entered without a time is stored as local midnight of the uploader's browser, converted to UTC."
  },
